    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You</strong> are a photographer in a Japanese Classroom armed with only your camera and wits. Capture photo's of anomalies to escape<strong>\u00a0CLASSROOM 9.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Photograph any anomalies you notice.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Keep an eye out for changes no matter how subtle or obvious.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Will you capture all the anomalies or fall victim to CLASSROOM 9?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A short liminal psychological horror game set in a Japanese classroom where you have to take photos of any anomalies you see in an everchanging room. Take your time and see how the room changes after every photo you take. A notice to detail and good memory will be helpful in completing this game.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong><i><u>Play Time</u></i></strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >30 - 90 minutes.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong><i><u>Controls</u></i></strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>WASD -</strong>\u00a0Basic movement (walk forwards, backwards, left, right).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Q -</strong> Pull out/ put away camera.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>E -</strong> Take a photo.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong><i><u>Language</u></i></strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game is only available in English but if you can read this you will have no trouble with the language. If you cannot understand English the game is still playable as there is very little need to know English anyway as long as you can find the play button.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Made with the capabilities of UE5.</i></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You</strong> are a photographer in a Japanese Classroom armed with only your camera and wits. Capture photo's of anomalies to escape<strong>\u00a0CLASSROOM 9.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Photograph any anomalies you notice.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Keep an eye out for changes no matter how subtle or obvious.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Will you capture all the anomalies or fall victim to CLASSROOM 9?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A short liminal psychological horror game set in a Japanese classroom where you have to take photos of any anomalies you see in an everchanging room. Take your time and see how the room changes after every photo you take. A notice to detail and good memory will be helpful in completing this game.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong><i><u>Play Time</u></i></strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >30 - 90 minutes.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong><i><u>Controls</u></i></strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>WASD -</strong>\u00a0Basic movement (walk forwards, backwards, left, right).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Q -</strong> Pull out/ put away camera.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>E -</strong> Take a photo.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong><i><u>Language</u></i></strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game is only available in English but if you can read this you will have no trouble with the language. If you cannot understand English the game is still playable as there is very little need to know English anyway as long as you can find the play button.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Made with the capabilities of UE5.</i></p>",
